called project 1. Duplicating a project numbers its copy from 1 (several videos, OS 1.1.x).",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":46},"new-confirm","The guide mentions no confirmation step for a new project, and it does not say what happens to unsaved changes when autosave is off; with autosave off, save with `M2` first.","derived",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":50,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"new-sounds","A new project starts with drums on tracks 1 and 2, then bass, pluck, lead, soft pluck, strings and pad on tracks 3–8.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/get-started#4.%20get%20started",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"save","`M2` saves the project and stores a version of it.",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"save-as","`shift + M2` saves a copy under a new name you type in.",{"id":58,"text":59,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"rename","`M3` renames the project: `turn E1` picks the character position and `turn E2` changes the character.",{"id":61,"text":62,"source":63,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"rename-keys","In the naming screen, `M1` confirms, `M2` moves on to the next character, `M3` cancels and `M4` deletes.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#view-and-create-preset",{"id":65,"text":66,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"config","`M4` opens the project settings, which are separate from the system settings.",[68,79],{"id":32,"goal":69,"preconditions":70,"steps":71,"result":75,"source":76,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":77,"confidence":78},"Start a new project",[],[72,73],{"keys":12,"note":24,"set":24},{"keys":74,"note":24,"set":24},"hold M1","A new project opens with the default sounds.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133","1.